{
 "about": "Labelled returns for the demo and the evaluation. Products are real catalog SKUs (milistu/AMAZON-Products-2023). Orders, customers, reasons and dock photos are synthetic: dock photos are generated from the catalog image (cut-out, warehouse surface, rotation, lighting, optional crack/scratch overlay) or from a Wikimedia image. The agent never sees the `gt` block.",
 "rubric": [
  "Item in the photo is not the ordered product -> ESCALATE (possible return fraud).",
  "Intact item returned for packaging damage, cosmetic reasons or change of mind -> RESTOCK as open box.",
  "Functional defect claim, new item from a vendor with RTV terms, inside the window, price < $300 -> RETURN_TO_VENDOR.",
  "Functional claim on an item >= $300 that the photos cannot verify -> ESCALATE for a human bench check, unless a human precedent covers the same situation.",
  "Visible damage on a repairable device where repair is well below resale value -> REFURBISH.",
  "Otherwise (low value, not repairable, repair costs more than it recovers) -> LIQUIDATE.",
  "Ground-truth grade = visible condition in the dock photo: intact photo -> A, crack or scratch overlay -> C (grade is not scored for mismatched items)."
 ],
